  "behavior": [
    "One safe TextEncoding domain with GNU native0/UTF8=1/Latin1=2/bytes3/symbol5/any99 adapters; preserve the actual serialized GP mask bits and GNU getCharCE precedence.",
    "Migrate all getCharCE ordinal comparisons and graphics/grid/native helper constants to that domain. Byte Rstrwid now uses GNU bytes3 and four hex columns for e9.",
    "Use checked sealed payload leases for native-compatible text, with no extra copy; Latin1/native-C conversions own fallible exact-length buffers and original-heap transient tickets, including native terminators.",
    "Validate original heap domains, input shape, immutable data and bounded terminators before reads. Keep actual payload data and its charge alive after original arena teardown.",
    "Publish requested tags inside the original constructor lend before GC/provider notification; ASCII stays unknown, byte mode dominates, native/known/collapse tags follow GNU paste.",
    "Honor UTF8 sprintf arguments as well as formats, and reject byte translations including paste separators before coercion, as GNU does."
